1
00:01:08,079 --> 00:01:08,760
Who are you?

2
00:01:18,519 --> 00:01:19,159
They're right here.

3
00:01:19,879 --> 00:01:20,760
Hurry and move the firewood!

4
00:01:21,280 --> 00:01:21,680
Hurry!

5
00:01:22,079 --> 00:01:22,680
Come help!

6
00:01:23,439 --> 00:01:23,879
Hold on.

7
00:01:24,319 --> 00:01:25,560
If they're really hiding in there...

8
00:01:26,040 --> 00:01:27,719
...isn't doing this a bit impolite?

9
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,680
Stop going on and on about female ghosts.

10
00:01:29,799 --> 00:01:30,519
There are no ghosts.

11
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:32,680
There really is a ghost in the Li Mansion!

12
00:01:32,799 --> 00:01:34,400
My master and I saw it with our own eyes!

13
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:36,159
You've really seen a ghost?

14
00:01:36,359 --> 00:01:37,239
It's the absolute truth!

15
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:38,599
That female ghost was covered in blood...

16
00:01:38,719 --> 00:01:39,519
...and absolutely terrifying!

17
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:41,359
They aren't ghosts at all.

18
00:01:42,319 --> 00:01:42,920
They're human.

19
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:45,159
Three living, breathing people.

20
00:01:55,439 --> 00:01:57,280
The ghost was barely an inch away from me.

21
00:01:58,760 --> 00:02:00,040
I could feel her breath,

22
00:02:01,159 --> 00:02:02,120
her body heat,

23
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:05,159
and I could even smell

24
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:06,079
the powder on their faces.

25
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:10,360
When I thought about it later,

26
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:11,919
I was certain.

27
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:14,560
The so-called ghosts in the Li Mansion

28
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:16,400
were all just people in disguise.

29
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:17,479
See?

30
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:19,439
I told you

31
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:20,199
they weren't ghosts.

32
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:21,639
Why didn't you tell me earlier?

33
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:23,639
I was nearly scared to death!

34
00:02:26,599 --> 00:02:27,240
Since

35
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:29,840
they want to put on a show,

36
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:31,599
we'll play along

37
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:33,520
and be the audience

38
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:34,800
to watch the spectacle.

39
00:02:34,919 --> 00:02:35,400
Watch out!

40
00:02:39,199 --> 00:02:39,879
I had no idea

41
00:02:40,199 --> 00:02:41,639
you hid your skills so well.

42
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:42,960
You're pretty good.

43
00:02:46,039 --> 00:02:47,039
The magic trick you want to see

44
00:02:49,280 --> 00:02:50,000
is right inside.

45
00:03:01,599 --> 00:03:02,840
The First Madam's white dress.

46
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:04,840
The Second Madam's Western dress.

47
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:06,400
The Third Madam's costume.

48
00:03:07,319 --> 00:03:08,400
The ghosts were actually people in disguise.

49
00:03:12,159 --> 00:03:14,199
This is the rouge the First Madam used on her face.

50
00:03:15,319 --> 00:03:16,560
It has a high proportion of talcum powder.

51
00:03:17,439 --> 00:03:18,360
It's whiter than normal foundation.

52
00:03:19,120 --> 00:03:19,800
Specifically for theater troupes.

53
00:03:29,159 --> 00:03:30,560
And what's inside this bottle...

54
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,000
is red pigment made from cochineal.

55
00:03:33,599 --> 00:03:34,639
The blood on the Second Madam's head...

56
00:03:35,280 --> 00:03:36,199
was exactly this.

57
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:44,919
What is this?

58
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:46,759
This nail guard...

59
00:03:47,599 --> 00:03:48,479
is what the Third Madam...

60
00:03:49,080 --> 00:03:50,719
used as the ghost hand to scare Master Li.

61
00:03:53,840 --> 00:03:55,159
The women in the Li Mansion...

62
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:57,280
are only Chunmei and the shaman.

63
00:03:57,639 --> 00:03:59,000
And the servants are all men.

64
00:03:59,879 --> 00:04:01,639
So who played these three ghosts?

65
00:04:05,319 --> 00:04:05,879
Demoness.

66
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:08,319
We just arrived in Lijia Town.

67
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:09,639
We don't know much about this place.

68
00:04:10,439 --> 00:04:12,520
Did any theater troupes come to town to perform?

69
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:15,159
Last year.

70
00:04:15,919 --> 00:04:17,240
Last year, there was a...

71
00:04:17,399 --> 00:04:19,480
Western magic troupe that came here.

72
00:04:19,959 --> 00:04:22,199
Later, a Peking opera troupe and a Kunqu opera troupe came.

73
00:04:22,639 --> 00:04:23,680
What about last month?

74
00:04:24,079 --> 00:04:24,920
Which was...

75
00:04:25,079 --> 00:04:26,240
after the three madams died.

76
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:28,240
Did any troupes come then?

77
00:04:28,519 --> 00:04:29,160
Last month...

78
00:04:30,079 --> 00:04:31,040
Last month...

79
00:04:32,120 --> 00:04:32,879
I remember now.

80
00:04:33,319 --> 00:04:34,800
An acrobatics troupe came.

81
00:04:34,879 --> 00:04:36,199
Let me tell you, they...

82
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:37,360
They are from the acrobatics troupe.

83
00:04:38,839 --> 00:04:39,319
Furthermore,

84
00:04:39,959 --> 00:04:40,959
they are masters in the Art of disguise.

85
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:43,040
The so-called Art of disguise...

86
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:45,279
can alter bone structure and conceal the skin.

87
00:04:45,959 --> 00:04:46,800
Eyebrows and eyes can be drawn.

88
00:04:47,079 --> 00:04:47,839
Wrinkles can be added.

89
00:04:49,199 --> 00:04:51,240
That's how they used makeup and the Art of disguise

90
00:04:51,839 --> 00:04:52,920
to disguise themselves as female ghosts.

91
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:55,279
They played the female ghosts!

92
00:04:56,839 --> 00:04:58,199
If the ghosts were played by people...

93
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:00,639
Where did those strange noises at night come from?

94
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:02,879
Run!

95
00:05:03,079 --> 00:05:03,879
The ghost is here!

96
00:05:04,040 --> 00:05:04,920
The ghost is here!

97
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:08,399
A Gramophone recording?

98
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:09,560
It wasn't a recording.

99
00:05:11,319 --> 00:05:13,360
A Gramophone has a single sound source,

100
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:15,360
but these strange sounds...

101
00:05:15,879 --> 00:05:17,240
came from all directions.

102
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:20,720
Then where did the sounds come from?

103
00:05:20,959 --> 00:05:21,879
Sound is produced...

104
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:22,959
by the vibration of objects.

105
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:25,480
So we should search the entire mansion

106
00:05:26,079 --> 00:05:27,160
thoroughly.

107
00:05:27,319 --> 00:05:28,519
See if there's anything unusual.

108
00:05:29,079 --> 00:05:31,720
Then we can find the source of these strange sounds.

109
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:32,920
What exactly are we looking for?

110
00:05:35,519 --> 00:05:36,240
Look for small holes.

111
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:37,240
Small holes?

112
00:05:45,279 --> 00:05:45,759
Master.

113
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:48,040
Are these the small holes you mentioned?

114
00:05:48,839 --> 00:05:49,319
Exactly.

115
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:51,040
It's these...

116
00:05:51,519 --> 00:05:53,040
round holes piercing through the walls.

117
00:05:54,040 --> 00:05:55,399
There are nine small holes in total here.

118
00:05:56,319 --> 00:05:57,839
Why would they drill holes in the wall?

119
00:05:58,279 --> 00:05:59,120
What's the principle behind this?

120
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:01,920
The strange sounds being produced...

121
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:03,759
originated from these small holes.

122
00:06:05,199 --> 00:06:06,959
These small holes can make sounds?

123
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:08,519
Have you ever played a harmonica?

124
00:06:10,519 --> 00:06:12,000
According to the construction principles of the Classic of Lu Ban,

125
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:13,399
they turned the Li Mansion

126
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:15,000
into a giant harmonica.

127
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,519
The outer walls are higher than the inner courtyard,

128
00:06:18,279 --> 00:06:20,240
which facilitates air resonance.

129
00:06:21,759 --> 00:06:22,680
They also carved

130
00:06:22,920 --> 00:06:24,040
small holes like these into the walls,

131
00:06:24,439 --> 00:06:26,240
just like the sound holes in a harmonica.

132
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:28,439
When the north wind blows through,

133
00:06:28,920 --> 00:06:30,480
the wind causes resonance,

134
00:06:30,879 --> 00:06:33,079
which produces these strange sounds.

135
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:46,360
Madam.

136
00:06:47,079 --> 00:06:48,079
You're finally back.

137
00:06:48,160 --> 00:06:49,199
I was worried sick.

138
00:06:49,319 --> 00:06:50,360
Where did you run off to?

139
00:06:50,439 --> 00:06:51,480
What do you care where I went?

140
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:53,839
Madam, the auspicious hour is near.

141
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,199
Let's hurry up and perform the wedding ceremony.

142
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:57,240
Benefactor Li.

143
00:06:58,120 --> 00:06:59,639
Don't you want to know who wants to kill you?

144
00:07:00,639 --> 00:07:01,160
Madam...

145
00:07:01,759 --> 00:07:02,879
You found the killer?

146
00:07:03,319 --> 00:07:04,199
At this very moment,

147
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:05,319
the killer is in the Li Mansion.

148
00:07:05,879 --> 00:07:06,959
We've already searched outside.

149
00:07:07,279 --> 00:07:07,959
Only the inside is left.

150
00:07:08,639 --> 00:07:09,759
The Li Mansion is your home.

151
00:07:10,399 --> 00:07:11,040
Search all you want.

152
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:31,680
This silver needle

153
00:07:32,480 --> 00:07:34,759
is the hidden weapon used to assassinate Mengzhu.

154
00:07:35,879 --> 00:07:36,439
Earlier,

155
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:40,000
it was used on the Zhong Kui puppet.

156
00:07:40,920 --> 00:07:41,680
And in the woods,

157
00:07:41,759 --> 00:07:42,240
Watch out!

158
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:43,639
it was the weapon used to assassinate me.

159
00:07:45,279 --> 00:07:46,319
These paints and brushes

160
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:49,560
were used by the killer to paint the boy's portrait.

161
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:51,040
He's over there!

162
00:07:53,199 --> 00:07:54,120
And this pair of shoes

163
00:07:54,639 --> 00:07:57,079
matches the shape of the shoes found at the crime scene,

164
00:07:57,199 --> 00:07:58,279
as well as the sole patterns

165
00:07:58,639 --> 00:07:59,560
perfectly.

166
00:08:00,519 --> 00:08:01,040
The killer

167
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:03,160
was wearing these exact shoes

168
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:05,040
when attempting to assassinate me.

169
00:08:06,519 --> 00:08:07,319
All these items

170
00:08:07,959 --> 00:08:09,560
were found in Chunmei's room.

171
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:12,680
Before Mengzhu and the three madams died,

172
00:08:13,199 --> 00:08:14,480
they were all served by Chunmei.

173
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:16,399
Therefore,

174
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:17,680
the killer

175
00:08:18,560 --> 00:08:19,279
is Chunmei.

176
00:08:24,079 --> 00:08:25,040
Oh, Chunmei,

177
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:28,000
I've always treated you so well.

178
00:08:28,839 --> 00:08:31,199
Why did you kill Mengzhu and the others?

179
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:32,960
Could someone be framing Chunmei?

180
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:35,240
Chunmei,

181
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:37,759
you're suspected of killing four women in the Li Mansion,

182
00:08:38,519 --> 00:08:39,919
and making multiple failed attempts on Jiang Huai's life.

183
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:40,840
Come with me to the police station.

184
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:41,440
I want to turn myself in.

185
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:43,279
I want to turn myself in too.

186
00:08:44,559 --> 00:08:45,279
Dazhu, Erzhu.

187
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:46,360
What does this have to do with you?

188
00:08:46,519 --> 00:08:47,120
Hurry back!

189
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:48,159
Why is it you guys?

190
00:08:48,879 --> 00:08:49,360
Inspector,

191
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:50,799
you've arrested the wrong person.

192
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:52,919
Chunmei is just a weak woman.

193
00:08:53,320 --> 00:08:54,039
She couldn't kill anyone.

194
00:08:54,919 --> 00:08:56,600
I killed the madams and the young lady.

195
00:08:57,159 --> 00:08:57,919
Let Chunmei go.

196
00:08:58,639 --> 00:09:00,600
You're not the stuttering Erzhu.

197
00:09:00,679 --> 00:09:01,240
Inspector Mu,

198
00:09:01,960 --> 00:09:02,919
don't listen to his nonsense.

199
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:04,759
He doesn't have what it takes to kill anyone.

200
00:09:05,399 --> 00:09:07,240
I killed them.

201
00:09:07,279 --> 00:09:07,840
Big brother.

202
00:09:09,159 --> 00:09:10,159
The one who tried to assassinate Jiang Huai

203
00:09:11,320 --> 00:09:11,960
was also me.

204
00:09:13,159 --> 00:09:14,840
You're not the submissive Dazhu.

205
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:17,240
What do you mean, submissive?

206
00:09:18,440 --> 00:09:19,639
I can see he has profound inner strength.

207
00:09:20,799 --> 00:09:22,519
He must be the best martial artist in the Li Mansion, right?

208
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:24,000
That's right.

209
00:09:28,639 --> 00:09:29,600
The eldest brother, Dazhu,

210
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:31,200
a security guard at the furniture factory.

211
00:09:31,919 --> 00:09:32,519
He's highly skilled,

212
00:09:33,559 --> 00:09:35,039
and excels in woodworking and painting.

213
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:36,840
The second brother, Erzhu,

214
00:09:37,519 --> 00:09:38,679
is a worker at the chemical plant.

215
00:09:39,919 --> 00:09:40,919
Besides growing flowers,

216
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:42,600
he also knows how to make Caustic Soda.

217
00:09:44,240 --> 00:09:45,039
The third sister, Chunmei,

218
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:46,960
is a female worker at the textile mill.

219
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:48,440
She excels at sewing.

220
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:51,840
The madams of the Li Mansion

221
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:53,840
trusted her deeply.

222
00:09:54,919 --> 00:09:56,200
It was the three of them

223
00:09:56,480 --> 00:09:58,320
who collaborated from the inside and out to commit the crimes.

224
00:09:59,039 --> 00:09:59,919
Jiang Huai,

225
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:02,039
you really are a brilliant strategist.

226
00:10:02,639 --> 00:10:03,639
You three, come with me to the police station.

227
00:10:03,639 --> 00:10:04,080
Wait.

228
00:10:06,759 --> 00:10:07,279
Don't forget,

229
00:10:08,919 --> 00:10:09,879
there are still some who slipped through the net.

230
00:10:10,600 --> 00:10:11,440
There's someone else?

231
00:10:14,799 --> 00:10:15,639
The three female ghosts.

232
00:10:16,759 --> 00:10:17,759
Come out on your own.
